  "summary": "Order ORD-10482 (Halden H2 headphones, 120.00 USD, completed payment) was shipped Oct 29, 2026 via Meridian Parcel Service Ground, tracking MP-4821-7731-0042, to the same ship-to address as on the PayPal record. Carrier tracking shows the shipment was never delivered: a delivery attempt failed Nov 3 for no access, it was marked undeliverable Nov 4, and it was returned to sender in Portland, OR on Nov 6, 2026. The buyer contacted support on Nov 7 and Nov 11, 2026 saying she had not received the headphones and had opened the PayPal inquiry. Store policy states that when a carrier returns an order as undeliverable, the full order total is refunded once the return scan appears on the carrier's tracking page, with no action needed from the customer. The customer has 2 previous orders, so the repeat-claims clause asking for more detail before any goodwill offer also applies, though the no-signature-delivery clause is not applicable since there is no delivery scan. There were no earlier refunds on this payment.",
